# Line endings and encoding are load-bearing in this project -- see the README
# section "仓库里的 .gitattributes 为什么写得那么怪". Do not "simplify" these
# rules, and do not let a tool strip them.

# Default for everything not matched below: normalise to LF in the repository
# and in the working tree, so no per-machine core.autocrlf setting can change
# what a contributor ends up with.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files MUST keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them. The .bat files
# here are deliberately ASCII-only, so a text rule is safe for them.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The .ps1 files are deliberately BOM-prefixed UTF-8: Windows PowerShell 5.1
# reads a BOM-less .ps1 as GBK, which mangles the Chinese UI strings and can even
# cause parse errors. `binary` makes git store and check out the exact bytes --
# no BOM stripping, no newline conversion, no autocrlf/AutoCrlf surprises.
*.ps1 binary

# Binary artefacts
*.docx binary
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
